# Single-Stage Common-Source Amplifier with Current-Source Load

A high-gain, high-bandwidth single-stage Common-Source (CS) analog amplifier designed and simulated in **Cadence Virtuoso** using the **GPDK90 (90nm)** Process Design Kit (PDK). 

This design implements a wide NMOS driver coupled with a PMOS active current-source load to maximize output impedance (\(r_o\)) and maximize small-signal voltage gain without relying on passive resistive loads.

---

## 🛠️ Circuit Schematic & Architecture

The amplifier consists of a standard NMOS driver (`NM0`) operating under a fixed power rail, loaded by a PMOS current source (`PM0`) biased in the saturation region.

*   **Technology Node:** GPDK90 (90nm CMOS)
*   **Supply Voltage (\(V_{DD}\)):** 1.2 V
*   **Architecture:** Common-Source with PMOS Current-Source Load

### Transistor Sizing & Parameters

| Transistor | Instance Name | Model | Total Width (\(W\)) | Length (\(L\)) | Multiplicity (\(m\)) | Layout Strategy |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **NMOS Driver** | `NM0` | `nmos1v` | \(40\ \mu\text{m}\) | \(360\text{ nm}\) | 1 | Multi-finger (\(W_f = 5\ \mu\text{m}\), \(nf = 8\)) |
| **PMOS Load** | `PM0` | `pmos1v` | \(80\ \mu\text{m}\) | \(360\text{ nm}\) | 1 | Multi-finger (\(W_f = 5\ \mu\text{m}\), \(nf = 16\)) |

---

## 📈 Bias & Simulation Specifications

To guarantee symmetric maximum output voltage swing and keep both transistors locked firmly in **Saturation (Region 2)**, the following bias conditions were established via DC analysis sweeps:

### DC Operating Points

*   **\(V_{DD}\) Power Rail:** `1.2 V`
*   **PMOS Bias Voltage (\(V_{bias}\)):** `750 mV`
*   **NMOS Input DC Bias (\(V_{in,DC}\)):** `444.26 mV` *(Determined via mid-supply transfer curve alignment)*
*   **Quiescent Output Voltage (\(V_{out,DC}\)):** `596.32 mV` \(\approx V_{DD}/2\)

### Testbench Signal Configuration (`vsin`)
*   **DC Voltage:** `444.26 mV`
*   **AC Magnitude:** `1 V`
*   **Transient Amplitude:** `5 mV` (\(10\text{ mV}_{\text{peak-to-peak}}\))
*   **Input Frequency:** `1 kHz` *(Transient Test)* / Full Spectrum Sweep *(AC Test)*

---

## 🚀 Performance Summary & Optimization Results

The circuit underwent geometric optimization to combat deep sub-micron short-channel non-idealities (specifically **Channel Length Modulation**). Increasing the channel length and scaling widths proportionally yielded a substantial increase in output resistance (\(r_o\)) and voltage gain.

### Comparison: Baseline vs. Optimized Design

| Design Phase | Transistor Dimensions (\(W/L\)) | DC Input Bias (\(V_{in}\)) | Transient Output (\(V_{out, p-p}\)) | Voltage Gain (\(A_v\)) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Initial Baseline** | NMOS: \(20\ \mu\text{m} / 180\text{ nm}\)<br>PMOS: \(40\ \mu\text{m} / 180\text{ nm}\) | `412.00 mV` | \(76.52\text{ mV}\) | **`7.652`** (\(17.67\text{ dB}\)) |
| **Optimized Stage** | NMOS: \(40\ \mu\text{m} / 360\text{ nm}\)<br>PMOS: \(80\ \mu\text{m} / 360\text{ nm}\) | `444.26 mV` | \(198.75\text{ mV}\) | **`19.938`** (\(26.02\text{ dB}\)) |

### Final Verified Performance Metrics
*   **3dB Cutoff Frequency (\(f_{-3\text{dB}}\)):** **`720 MHz`**
*   **True Gain-Bandwidth Product (GBW):** **`14.399 GHz`** (\(\text{Gain}_{\text{linear}} \times f_{-3\text{dB}}\))
*   **Signal Integrity:** Perfectly smooth, undistorted transient output wave with zero voltage rail clipping or compression.
